<%# A debate's entry in the hoojah "Debates" lens. Links to the transcript screen.
    Local: debate.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.5) —
    docs/design-system/components/debate/DebateCard.prompt.md. The card surface comes
    from `ds_card_classes` rather than `ui/_card`, because this card IS the link: it
    carries `href`, a `dom_id` and the `.debate-card` hook a system spec selects on, and
    `ui/_card` has no `href:` local by design. Its own header names this file as the
    documented escape hatch — "If your card IS a link … call `ds_card_classes` directly
    on the `link_to` instead."

    `padded:` is NOT used. DebateCard.jsx sets `padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4)`,
    i.e. `px-4 py-2`, and the helper's `padded:` is the taller `px-4 py-3` of a hujah
    card. Mixing the two is the trap `ui/_card`'s header spells out — same-family
    utilities resolve by bundle order, so `py-3` would silently beat the `py-2` this row
    wants. Spell the padding, omit the flag.

    The state colours are FIXED (DebateCard.prompt.md: pending → agree orange, active →
    indigo, concluded → grey, declined → light-grey) and the label is a 12px uppercase
    `tracking-wide` micro-label — the same treatment as the verdict heading and the turn
    phase caption. `text-<state>` is INTERPOLATED, so the four tones behind it live in
    the `@source inline` safelist in app/assets/tailwind/application.css; all four are
    already covered there by the stance and grey lines. The map is duplicated in the
    sibling `_debate_status` on purpose: that partial renders in a BROADCAST context and
    the two files may not share a request-only seam. %>
<% state_color = {"pending" => "agree", "active" => "primary", "concluded" => "grey", "declined" => "light-grey"}[debate.status] || "grey" %>
<%= link_to debate_path(debate.slug), id: dom_id(debate, :card),
      class: "#{ds_card_classes} debate-card no-underline px-4 py-2 flex items-center justify-between" do %>
  <span class="flex items-center gap-1 text-black fill-neutral min-w-0">
    <%= lucide_icon("swords", class: "w-4 h-4 shrink-0") %>
    <span class="truncate">@<%= debate.challenger.username %> vs @<%= debate.opponent.username %></span>
  </span>
  <span class="debate-state shrink-0 ml-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-<%= state_color %>">
    <%= debate.status.titleize %>
  </span>
<% end %>
